// The compiler injects these helpers into std::os_abi with pub(root) visibility:
// only the std package can use them. Signatures below are documentation, not
// source declarations. They implement the Linux x86-64 pointer/register boundary
// and do not provide a public pointer/integer conversion API.
//
// pub(root) fn pointer_from_word(T: type, word: uint64) *T
// Interpret a register word as an address of T. Pass T explicitly; no allocation,
// dereference, alignment, capacity or lifetime validation occurs. A zero word
// produces a null pointer. The caller must establish validity before access.
// Example within std: root::os_abi::pointer_from_word(uint8, word)
//
// pub(root) fn pointer_to_word(pointer: *T) uint64
// pub(root) fn pointer_to_word(pointer: const *T) uint64
// Return the pointer's address as a register word without accessing storage.
// T is inferred; no separate type argument is passed. The result retains no
// readonly or lifetime information, so std callers must preserve those contracts
// when reconstructing pointers. A null pointer produces zero.
// Example within std: root::os_abi::pointer_to_word(pointer)
